<title>INDIA: India frees investments in funds from capital tax.</title>
<headline>India frees investments in funds from capital tax.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said on Friday investments in all mutual funds will be exempted from capital gains tax.  </p>
<p>&quot;Under section 54 EA of the Income Tax Act which I have proposed in the Finance Bill under consideration, capital gains exemption is to be given if the investment is made for three years in bonds or debentures notified by Central Board of Direct Taxes (CBDT,&quot; Chidambaram told the parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;I propose to expand the coverage to include investment in all mutual funds,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
